      "title": "Examples of Vector Product",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "e2c5c034-041b-5340-9823-5e3c8c88a07c",
          "pdf_from": 25,
          "pdf_to": 28,
          "note": "Examples of Vector Product: a main subheading of 2.3 Product of two vectors, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 25-28."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "When a force F⃗ is applied on a rigid body at a point whose position vector is r from any point on the axis about which the body rotates, then the turning effect of the force called the torque τ is given by the vector product of r⃗ and F⃗."
            ],
            "marker": "i."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{\\tau} = \\vec{r}\\times\\vec{F}",
            "text_alt": "τ⃗ = r⃗ × F⃗"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "The force F⃗ on a particle of charge q and velocity v⃗ in a magnetic field of strength B⃗ is given by vector product of v⃗ and B⃗."
            ],
            "marker": "i.",
            "start": 2
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{F} = q(\\vec{v}\\times\\vec{B})",
            "text_alt": "F⃗ = q(v⃗ × B⃗)"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
